Engine: the original's view kept round a commanded battle action (open fix 65).

STATUS: APPLIED 1 October 2026 by work order 197 (Part B.2, "exercise ...
correct what is off") — orion2re 76c7b880 on orionlayer-local (before:
ee844b0b), this file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required
by tools/version_check.py since work order 197.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_combat_command_view.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 76c7b880` or `patch -R -p1`,
and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    A clicking player can choose only a cell inside the original's 32 x 18
    view, which the game centres on the acting ship at its turn; open fix
    58's MOVE can name any legal cell. In work order 197's battle at Altair
    (the armed scratch game) a Doom Star holding a tractor beam was moved by
    command to a cell beyond the view and the engine died: Move_Ship_ draws
    the moving ship at its view position, and while it holds a tractor beam
    it first redraws the whole battle (Draw_Main_Combat_Screen_), which ends
    with Clip_Off_; the ship, partly outside the view, was then drawn
    unclipped outside the frame buffer — SIGSEGV in draw::Draw_Bitmap_Sprite_
    at (-76, -78), twice (cores of PIDs 582033, 582848).

    Now MOVE, FIRE and BOARD centre the original's view on the middle of
    the action with the game's own COMBINIT::Snap_Center_Combat_Screen_
    (the C key's and every turn's centring) before the action runs, and a
    MOVE longer than the view less a ship's margin (26 x 12 cells) is
    refused (reason 10, new). The original builds a missile's field only
    while the missile is inside its view (combat1.cpp:436-455), so the same
    battle refused FIRE_MISSILE at an enemy missile outside it (reason 8):
    now the view is centred on the missile and the battle's fields rebuilt
    first (the game's own COMBAT1::Add_Tactical_Combat_Fields_), and fix
    58's check follows as before. Only the hidden original view moves — the one a
    player would have scrolled to make the click; nothing of the battle
    does. The engine's own clipping gap stays as it is (an engine fix that
    changes the game without OrionLayer: parked for Data).

    Written only in src/ext, inside open fix 58's Take_Combat_Command;
    nothing runs unless a client sends a command, so an engine without
    OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix
    65.`, on one line at each changed place.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 5d754c6a..24c30e35 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -2261,6 +2261,28 @@ void Combat_Event(uint8_t type, int16_t a0, int16_t a1, int16_t a2, int16_t a3,
     ++g_combat_event_next;
 }
 
+// OrionLayer, open fix 65. The original's view kept round a commanded action, as a player's click keeps it.
+// A clicking player can only choose a cell inside the original's view, which
+// the game centres on the acting ship at its turn; a command can name any
+// legal cell. Move_Ship_ draws the moving ship at its view position, and
+// while it holds a tractor beam it redraws the whole battle first
+// (Draw_Main_Combat_Screen_), which switches clipping off, so a ship partly
+// outside the view was drawn unclipped outside the frame buffer: SIGSEGV
+// (work order 197, the armed scratch game at Altair). So the view is centred
+// on the middle of the action with the game's own Snap_Center_Combat_Screen_
+// before the action runs, and a move longer than the view less a ship's
+// margin (26 x 12 cells of 32 x 18) is refused (reason 10). The original
+// builds a missile's field only while the missile is inside its view
+// (combat1.cpp:436-455), so FIRE_MISSILE at one outside it centres the view
+// on the missile and rebuilds the battle's fields first (the game's own
+// Add_Tactical_Combat_Fields_). Only the hidden original view moves;
+// nothing of the battle does.
+static bool Keep_Action_In_View_(int16_t x0, int16_t y0, int16_t x1, int16_t y1, bool refuse_long) {
+    if (refuse_long && (abs(x1 - x0) > 26 || abs(y1 - y0) > 12)) return false;
+    COMBINIT::Snap_Center_Combat_Screen_((int16_t)((x0 + x1) / 2), (int16_t)((y0 + y1) / 2));
+    return true;
+}
